\title{quicopt: Client for the 'Quicopt' Optimization Service}
\description{
Write an optimization model in R and solve it with the 'Quicopt' service \url{https://quicopt.com}: state the decisions, the objective and the constraints, and the service finds the best decision. The model is sent to the service, so no solver needs to be installed. Uncertain data, such as demand or prices, is described by probability distributions or taken from the rows of a data frame, and the model can then minimize an expected cost, guard against bad outcomes, or require a condition to hold with a given probability. Decisions that are an order or an assignment, such as a delivery route, can be stated directly.
